  "gaps": [
    "The 26-credit remaining general education block is derived (45 total minus 15 required course credits minus the 4-credit ENG minimum); the capture states only the 45-credit total, the required courses, and the ENG minimum. Listed ENG courses carry 6 credits, so the actual ENG/remaining split may differ.",
    "General education also requires a minimum of 4 quarter credits from each category (Communication, Humanities, Natural Science and Mathematics, Social Science); per-category fulfillment is not itemized in the ledger.",
    "ACS1003 (6 quarter credits) is required only for students determined to need additional writing/reading support; the capture does not state whether it counts within the 180-credit total. Blocks of 45+36+36+57+6 already sum to 180 without it.",
    "Footnote § states students who completed ACS1003 choose 57 quarter credits of electives—the same amount—so it is unclear how ACS1003 affects elective credits.",
    "The capture does not state whether a PSYC2700/PSYC2720/PSYC2740 course taken for the core choice may also count toward the 12-credit specialization list.",
    "Total requires a minimum of 54 quarter credits at the 3000-level and above; this upper-division constraint is not represented as a separate ledger line.",
    "Honors Pathway students complete PHI-H2005 (3), COM-H4005 (6), and SOC-H3005 (6) (at least 15 quarter credits), applied toward general education; this optional variant is not itemized.",
    "FlexPath delivery uses program points rather than quarter credits; the FlexPath version of this program is not captured here.",
    "No residency or institutional-credit (must-complete-at-Capella) requirement is stated in the capture.",
    "Course prerequisites are referenced but not detailed in the capture."
  ],
